# Ecosystem boundaries

## Layout

| Path | Access |
|------|--------|
| `~/ai/agents/architectagent/` | Read/write (home) |
| `~/ai/agents/*/AGENTS.md` | Read (handoff targets) |
| User-attached project repo(s) | Read (explore); **no write** unless user explicitly grants for docs-only paths |
| `~/ai/status/` | Read/write **only when user grants** (INDEX, daily log, own snapshot) |
| `~/ai/tools/` | No — unless user grants |

## Required behavior

1. **Ask** repo paths and permissions every session.
2. **Do not assume** access to other agents' `plans/` or private agents.
3. Handoffs reference **agent role names** and what each agent may do — read their `AGENTS.md`.
4. Follow shared tracking via `02-shared-tracking.mdc` when status access is granted.

## Publishing

**Visibility: public** — agent folder may export to `role-based-agent-model-harness` except `plans/` (agent-publisher enforces).
